records.rationale:
In `AssertEvents.isAccessTokenId`, `matchesSafely` does `items[0].substring(3, 5)` after only checking `items.length != 2`. There is no guard that `items[0].length() >= 5`, so a token id like `"a:b"` (or any prefix shorter than 5 chars) would throw `StringIndexOutOfBoundsException` inside the matcher instead of returning `false`.

```java
if (items.length != 2) return false;
// no length check for items[0]
if (items[0].substring(3, 5).equals(expectedGrantShortcut)) return false;
```
